---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import FeatureRow from "../components/FeatureRow.astro";
import Shot from "../components/Shot.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Calendar and Training Library"
  description="Plan your training in Heracles Records: a calendar of planned and done, your COROS workouts and plans, and one builder for every sport. Everything saves to your COROS account."
>
  <section class="wrap page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Plan</p>
    <h1>Plan it here, and your watch has it.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Your COROS calendar, workouts and plans, with room to read and build them. Everything you
      save goes straight to your COROS account, so it is on your watch the next time it syncs.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section-tight">
    <Shot name="09-calendar" alt="Calendar: planned and completed sessions by month" eager />
  </section>

  <div class="wrap">
    <FeatureRow shot="21-calendar-detail" alt="Calendar with a session's detail open beside the month">
      <p class="eyebrow">Calendar</p>
      <h2>Planned and done, side by side.</h2>
      <p>
        Every scheduled workout and every completed activity, by month or by week, matched to
        each other so a session shows how much of its plan you did.
      </p>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li><strong>Open any day.</strong> A session opens beside the month with its route, elevation and laps; a busy day opens as a whole.</li>
        <li><strong>Drag to move.</strong> Drop a session on another day and it moves on your COROS calendar too. A session from a plan stays part of that plan.</li>
        <li><strong>Week by week.</strong> The week view adds its load, load ratio, time, distance and climb.</li>
        <li><strong>From the library.</strong> Put any workout on a day, or select several upcoming ones at once.</li>
        <li><strong>Ask Coach</strong> about a day, a week or a single session.</li>
      </ul>
    </FeatureRow>

    <FeatureRow shot="22-library-workouts" alt="Training Library: the workout list and a workout's step structure" flip>
      <p class="eyebrow">Training Library</p>
      <h2>Every workout you keep on COROS.</h2>
      <p>
        Your COROS workout library in one list, each workout read step by step: warm-up, the
        repeats, recoveries and cool-down, with the targets in your own zones.
      </p>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li><strong>Schedule</strong> a workout on a day from a month view that shows the week it lands in.</li>
        <li><strong>Edit, duplicate, tag</strong> and favourite, all saved to COROS.</li>
        <li><strong>Search and filter</strong> the list to find a workout fast.</li>
      </ul>
    </FeatureRow>

    <FeatureRow shot="23-workout-builder" alt="The workout builder: warm-up, training and cool-down steps with zone targets">
      <p class="eyebrow">Builder</p>
      <h2>One builder for every sport.</h2>
      <p>
        Run, ride, swim, strength and the rest are built in the same place, step by step, with
        repeat groups for intervals.
      </p>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li><strong>Targets in your zones.</strong> Pick a heart-rate, pace or power zone and the builder shows what it means for you, from the thresholds on your COROS account.</li>
        <li><strong>Sensible from the first step.</strong> A new step starts with a length and an intensity that suit its sport and its place in the workout.</li>
        <li><strong>Strength from COROS's own catalogue</strong> of exercises, with sets, reps and weight.</li>
      </ul>
    </FeatureRow>

    <FeatureRow shot="10-library" alt="A 12-week marathon plan in the Training Library, week by week" flip>
      <p class="eyebrow">Plans</p>
      <h2>Multi-week plans, read and run.</h2>
      <p>
        Your COROS training plans, read week by week: the load of each week, the stages from
        base to taper, and every session in its day.
      </p>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li><strong>Edit</strong> sessions, weeks and stages, and keep a draft until you are ready to save it.</li>
        <li><strong>Add to calendar</strong> from a start date, with a preview of exactly which sessions land where.</li>
        <li><strong>See how it is going.</strong> Once a plan is running, each session shows whether it was done, and the plan its overall compliance.</li>
        <li><strong>Change a running plan</strong> and choose whether your calendar follows.</li>
      </ul>
    </FeatureRow>
  </div>

  <section class="wrap section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 class="section-title">Want a plan written for you?</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Ask Coach. It starts from a brief you can edit, draws an outline of the weeks, then writes
        every session to your zones. Read it in the Workbench, change what you like, and save it to
        COROS and your calendar like any other plan.
      </p>
      <a class="more" href="/coach">How Coach works</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .section-tight {
    padding-top: 40px;
  }
</style>
